</figure>

<figure xml:id="fig-lim-asymptote-diagonal">
<caption>
The path <m>y=x</m> from <xref ref="fig-lim-paths-interactive"/>,
lifted onto the surface. Since <m>f(x,x)=\frac12</m> for <m>x\ne0</m>,
the lifted path approaches height <m>\frac12</m>. The domain path is
shown on a lower reference plane to separate it from its surface trace;
the open circle marks a limiting position where the function is undefined.
This differs from the value along either axis, so the two-variable limit
does not exist.
</caption>
<image width="90%">
<shortdescription>A rotatable surface with the path y=x highlighted and its trace at height one half.</shortdescription>
<description><p>
The surface is z equals x y divided by x squared plus y squared, drawn
over a punctured disk with a small hole at the origin. The gold trace lies at height one half on both sides of the missing point over the origin, unlike the height zero traces along the axes.
A matching path is drawn on a reference plane below the surface, with
vertical guide lines connecting it to the trace. Arrows point inward
from both sides. Dragging rotates the diagram.
</p></description>
<asymptote label="asymptote-lim-diagonal"><![CDATA[
import graph3;
viewportmargin=(16,16);
// Retain interactive WebGL for HTML and vector graphics for print.
if(settings.outformat != "html") settings.render=0;
size(12cm,10cm);
triple eye=(4,-7,4);
currentprojection=orthographic(camera=eye,up=Z,target=(0,0,-0.25));
currentlight=light(gray(0.65),specularfactor=0.15,(4,-3,6),(-4,-1,3));

// xy/(x^2+y^2) = (1/2) sin(2 theta), independent of radius.
// Exclude r=0: the function has no value at the origin.
real inner=0.06, outer=1.7, floorZ=-1.05;
triple surfacePoint(pair p) {
  return (p.x*cos(p.y),p.x*sin(p.y),0.5*sin(2*p.y));
}
surface s=surface(surfacePoint,(inner,0),(outer,2*pi),8,96);
draw(s,surfacepen=gray(0.82)+opacity(0.25),
     meshpen=gray(0.65)+opacity(0.15)+linewidth(0.15pt));

// This lower grid is a diagrammatic copy of the domain, not z=0.
pen grid=gray(0.8)+linewidth(0.3pt);
for(int i=-3;i<=3;++i) {
  real u=0.55*i;
  draw((-1.8,u,floorZ)--(1.8,u,floorZ),grid);
  draw((u,-1.8,floorZ)--(u,1.8,floorZ),grid);
}
pen axisPen=gray(0.35)+linewidth(0.6pt);
draw(Label("$x$",1),(-1.9,0,floorZ)--(2.1,0,floorZ),axisPen,Arrow3);
draw(Label("$y$",1),(0,-1.9,floorZ)--(0,2.1,floorZ),axisPen,Arrow3);
draw(Label("$z$",1),(0,0,-0.65)--(0,0,1.0),axisPen+dashed,Arrow3);
label("$0$",(0,0,0),W,gray(0.35));
label("$\frac12$",(0,0,0.5),W,gray(0.35));

real theta=pi/4, level=0.5;
triple direction=(cos(theta),sin(theta),0);
pen accent=rgb("F0AC5F");
pen tracePen=accent+linewidth(2.6pt);
// Draw both halves separately so the highlighted trace never fills the hole.
for(int side=-1;side<=1;side+=2) {
  triple far=side*outer*direction;
  triple near=side*inner*direction;
  draw(far+floorZ*Z--near+floorZ*Z,accent+linewidth(1.8pt),Arrow3(size=5));
  draw(far+level*Z--near+level*Z,tracePen,Arrow3(size=5));
  for(int j=1;j<=5;++j) {
    triple v=side*(outer*j/5.5)*direction;
    draw(v+floorZ*Z--v+level*Z,accent+opacity(0.5)+dashed+linewidth(0.5pt));
  }
}
// A ring rather than a filled dot: this is a limit, not a defined value.
draw(circle((0,0,level),0.045,eye),accent+linewidth(1.4pt));
dot((0,0,floorZ),gray(0.35)+linewidth(3pt));
label("$(0,0)$",(0,0,floorZ),SW,gray(0.35));
label("$y=x$",1.55*direction+floorZ*Z+0.3*(sin(theta),-cos(theta),0),S,accent);
label("$f=\frac12$",-1.1*direction+(level+0.13)*Z,N,accent);
label("$z=\dfrac{xy}{x^2+y^2}$",(-2.1,1.5,1.0),E,gray(0.3));
currentpicture.addBox((-2.2,-2.2,-1.2),(2.2,2.2,1.35));
]]></asymptote>
</image>
</figure>
</section>
<section xml:id="sec-pd-definition">
<title>Definition of Partial Derivatives</title>
<p>
On the surface <m>z=f(x,y)=3-0.25x^2-0.45y^2</m>, hold <m>y=y_0</m>
fixed to obtain a curve whose tangent slope is <m>f_x(x_0,y_0)</m>.
Holding <m>x=x_0</m> fixed instead gives the tangent slope
<m>f_y(x_0,y_0)</m>. The figures compare these two traces at
<m>P=(0.5,0.5,2.825)</m>.
</p>
<figure xml:id="fig-pd-tangent-x">
<caption>
The curve <m>z = f(x,y_0)</m> cut from the surface by the vertical plane
<m>y = y_0</m>, and its tangent line at <m>P</m>. The slope of that
tangent line is <m>\left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}\right|_{(x_0,y_0)}</m>.
</caption>
<image width="86%">
<description>
<p>
A grey surface with a green curve drawn on it through a magenta point P.
The curve is the trace of the surface in the plane y equals y nought, and
a blue tangent line touches it at P. A legend in the top left corner names
the surface, the curve, the tangent line and the point P.
</p>
</description>
<latex-image><![CDATA[
\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\fontfamily{phv}\selectfont]
\begin{axis}[
  width=12cm, height=9cm,
  view={-35}{20},
  xmin=-2.3, xmax=2.3, ymin=-2.3, ymax=2.3, zmin=0, zmax=5.2,
  xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, zlabel={$z$},
  ticks=none, clip=false,
  legend cell align=left,
  legend style={
    at={(0.01,0.99)}, anchor=north west,
    draw=gray!50, fill=white, fill opacity=0.92, text opacity=1,
    row sep=1.5pt, inner sep=4pt, font=\fontfamily{phv}\selectfont,
  },
]
% the surface
\addplot3[surf, shader=flat, draw=gray!55, fill=gray!30,
          fill opacity=0.20, draw opacity=0.20, forget plot,
          domain=-2:2, y domain=-2:2, samples=15]
  {3 - 0.25*x^2 - 0.45*y^2};
% trace in the plane y = y0 (green)
% A white under-stroke separates the parabola from the surface mesh.
\addplot3[line width=2.4pt, green!55!black, forget plot,
          preaction={draw=white, line width=4.2pt, opacity=1},
          line cap=round, line join=round,
          domain=-2:2, samples=65, samples y=0]
  ({x},{0.5},{2.8875 - 0.25*x^2});
% tangent line in y = y0, slope df/dx = -0.25
\addplot3[very thick, cyan!60!black, forget plot,
          domain=-1.3:1.3, samples=2, samples y=0]
  ({0.5+x},{0.5},{2.825 - 0.25*x});
% the point P
\addplot3[only marks, mark=*, mark size=1.9, color=magenta, forget plot]
  coordinates {(0.5,0.5,2.825)};
\node[magenta, anchor=south west, font=\fontfamily{phv}\selectfont] at (axis cs:0.5,0.5,2.9) {$P$};
% the legend, built by hand so that the surface gets an entry too
\addlegendimage{area legend, draw=gray!55, fill=gray!30, fill opacity=0.20}
\addlegendentry{$z=f(x,y)$}
\addlegendimage{line width=2.4pt, green!55!black}
\addlegendentry{$z=f(x,y_0)$}
\addlegendimage{very thick, cyan!60!black}
\addlegendentry{Tangent line in $y=y_0$}
\addlegendimage{only marks, mark=*, mark size=1.9, color=magenta}
\addlegendentry{$P=(x_0,y_0,f(x_0,y_0))$}
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
]]></latex-image>
</image>
</figure>

<figure xml:id="fig-pd-tangent-x-asymptote">
<caption>
Asymptote copy of <xref ref="fig-pd-tangent-x"/>: the curve
<m>z=f(x,y_0)</m> and its tangent line in the plane <m>y=y_0</m>.
The tangent slope at <m>P</m> is <m>\left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}\right|_{(x_0,y_0)}</m>.
</caption>
<image width="86%">
<shortdescription>A grey surface with a green trace, a blue tangent line, and a magenta point P.</shortdescription>
<description><p>
The surface z equals 3 minus one quarter x squared minus 0.45 y squared.
The trace holds y fixed at 0.5 and passes through P at (0.5, 0.5, 2.825).
Its tangent line at P has slope minus 0.25.
</p></description>
<asymptote label="asymptote-pd-tangent-x"><![CDATA[
import graph3;
// Keep HTML interactive; use vector rendering only for print output.
if(settings.outformat != "html") settings.render=0;
size(12cm,9cm);
currentprojection=orthographic(camera=(-6,-8,4),up=Z);
currentlight=light(gray(0.6),specularfactor=0.2,(4,-3,6),(-4,-1,3));

triple surfacePoint(pair p) {
  return (p.x,p.y,3-0.25*p.x^2-0.45*p.y^2);
}
surface s=surface(surfacePoint,(-2,-2),(2,2),14,14);
draw(s,surfacepen=gray(0.75)+opacity(0.35),
     meshpen=gray(0.55)+opacity(0.4)+linewidth(0.3pt));

pen tracePen=rgb("008000")+linewidth(1.8pt);
pen tangentPen=rgb("009999")+linewidth(1.8pt);
draw(graph(new triple(real t) {return (t,0.5,2.8875-0.25*t^2);},-2,2),tracePen);
draw(graph(new triple(real t) {return (0.5+t,0.5,2.825-0.25*t);},-1.3,1.3),tangentPen);
triple P=(0.5,0.5,2.825);
dot(P,magenta+linewidth(5pt));
label("$P$",P+0.12Z,NE,magenta);

pen ax=gray(0.25)+linewidth(0.6pt);
draw(Label("$x$",1),(-2.3,-2.3,0)--(2.3,-2.3,0),ax,Arrow3);
draw(Label("$y$",1),(-2.3,-2.3,0)--(-2.3,2.3,0),ax,Arrow3);
draw(Label("$z$",1),(-2.3,-2.3,0)--(-2.3,-2.3,5.2),ax,Arrow3);

// Legend in the scene, with the same colours as the TikZ original.
label("$z=f(x,y)$",(-3,1.8,5.2),E,gray(0.4));
label("$z=f(x,y_0)$",(-3,1.8,4.7),E,tracePen);
label("Tangent line in $y=y_0$",(-3,1.8,4.2),E,tangentPen);
label("$P=(x_0,y_0,f(x_0,y_0))$",(-3,1.8,3.7),E,magenta);
]]></asymptote>
</image>
</figure>

<figure xml:id="fig-pd-tangent-y">
<caption>
The curve <m>z = f(x_0,y)</m> cut from the surface by the vertical plane
<m>x = x_0</m>, and its tangent line at <m>P</m>. The slope of that
tangent line is <m>\left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial y}\right|_{(x_0,y_0)}</m>.
</caption>
<image width="86%">
<description>
<p>
A grey surface with an amber curve drawn on it through a magenta point P.
The curve is the trace of the surface in the plane x equals x nought, and
a dark red tangent line touches it at P. A legend in the top left corner
names the surface, the curve, the tangent line and the point P.
</p>
</description>
<latex-image><![CDATA[
\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\fontfamily{phv}\selectfont]
\begin{axis}[
  width=12cm, height=9cm,
  view={-35}{20},
  xmin=-2.3, xmax=2.3, ymin=-2.3, ymax=2.3, zmin=0, zmax=5.2,
  xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, zlabel={$z$},
  ticks=none, clip=false,
  legend cell align=left,
  legend style={
    at={(0.01,0.99)}, anchor=north west,
    draw=gray!50, fill=white, fill opacity=0.92, text opacity=1,
    row sep=1.5pt, inner sep=4pt, font=\fontfamily{phv}\selectfont,
  },
]
% the surface
\addplot3[surf, shader=flat, draw=gray!55, fill=gray!30,
          fill opacity=0.20, draw opacity=0.20, forget plot,
          domain=-2:2, y domain=-2:2, samples=15]
  {3 - 0.25*x^2 - 0.45*y^2};
% trace in the plane x = x0 (amber)
% A white under-stroke separates the parabola from the surface mesh.
\addplot3[line width=2.4pt, orange!85!black, forget plot,
          preaction={draw=white, line width=4.2pt, opacity=1},
          line cap=round, line join=round,
          domain=-2:2, samples=65, samples y=0]
  ({0.5},{x},{2.9375 - 0.45*x^2});
% tangent line in x = x0, slope df/dy = -0.45
\addplot3[very thick, purple!60!black, forget plot,
          domain=-1.3:1.3, samples=2, samples y=0]
  ({0.5},{0.5+x},{2.825 - 0.45*x});
% the point P
\addplot3[only marks, mark=*, mark size=1.9, color=magenta, forget plot]
  coordinates {(0.5,0.5,2.825)};
\node[magenta, anchor=south west, font=\fontfamily{phv}\selectfont] at (axis cs:0.5,0.5,2.9) {$P$};
% the legend, built by hand so that the surface gets an entry too
\addlegendimage{area legend, draw=gray!55, fill=gray!30, fill opacity=0.20}
\addlegendentry{$z=f(x,y)$}
\addlegendimage{line width=2.4pt, orange!85!black}
\addlegendentry{$z=f(x_0,y)$}
\addlegendimage{very thick, purple!60!black}
\addlegendentry{Tangent line in $x=x_0$}
\addlegendimage{only marks, mark=*, mark size=1.9, color=magenta}
\addlegendentry{$P=(x_0,y_0,f(x_0,y_0))$}
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
]]></latex-image>
</image>
</figure>

<figure xml:id="fig-pd-tangent-y-asymptote">
<caption>
Asymptote copy of <xref ref="fig-pd-tangent-y"/>: the curve
<m>z=f(x_0,y)</m> and its tangent line in the plane <m>x=x_0</m>.
The tangent slope at <m>P</m> is <m>\left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial y}\right|_{(x_0,y_0)}</m>.
</caption>
<image width="86%">
<shortdescription>A grey surface with an amber trace, a purple tangent line, and a magenta point P.</shortdescription>
<description><p>
The surface z equals 3 minus one quarter x squared minus 0.45 y squared.
The trace holds x fixed at 0.5 and passes through P at (0.5, 0.5, 2.825).
Its tangent line at P has slope minus 0.45.
</p></description>
<asymptote label="asymptote-pd-tangent-y"><![CDATA[
import graph3;
// Keep HTML interactive; use vector rendering only for print output.
if(settings.outformat != "html") settings.render=0;
size(12cm,9cm);
currentprojection=orthographic(camera=(-6,-8,4),up=Z);
currentlight=light(gray(0.6),specularfactor=0.2,(4,-3,6),(-4,-1,3));

triple surfacePoint(pair p) {
  return (p.x,p.y,3-0.25*p.x^2-0.45*p.y^2);
}
surface s=surface(surfacePoint,(-2,-2),(2,2),14,14);
draw(s,surfacepen=gray(0.75)+opacity(0.35),
     meshpen=gray(0.55)+opacity(0.4)+linewidth(0.3pt));

pen tracePen=orange+linewidth(1.8pt);
pen tangentPen=rgb("660066")+linewidth(1.8pt);
draw(graph(new triple(real t) {return (0.5,t,2.9375-0.45*t^2);},-2,2),tracePen);
draw(graph(new triple(real t) {return (0.5,0.5+t,2.825-0.45*t);},-1.3,1.3),tangentPen);
triple P=(0.5,0.5,2.825);
dot(P,magenta+linewidth(5pt));
label("$P$",P+0.12Z,NE,magenta);

pen ax=gray(0.25)+linewidth(0.6pt);
draw(Label("$x$",1),(-2.3,-2.3,0)--(2.3,-2.3,0),ax,Arrow3);
draw(Label("$y$",1),(-2.3,-2.3,0)--(-2.3,2.3,0),ax,Arrow3);
draw(Label("$z$",1),(-2.3,-2.3,0)--(-2.3,-2.3,5.2),ax,Arrow3);

// Legend in the scene, with the same colours as the TikZ original.
label("$z=f(x,y)$",(-3,1.8,5.2),E,gray(0.4));
label("$z=f(x_0,y)$",(-3,1.8,4.7),E,tracePen);
label("Tangent line in $x=x_0$",(-3,1.8,4.2),E,tangentPen);
label("$P=(x_0,y_0,f(x_0,y_0))$",(-3,1.8,3.7),E,magenta);
]]></asymptote>
</image>
</figure>
</section>
